23b:["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"live_memory_veto"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"string"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"—"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"unset (off)"}],["$","td",null,{"children":["The name of a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"minimum"}]," platform property, usually ",["$","code",null,{"children":"memory_kb"}],", that the scheduler compares against the free memory each worker reports with its keepalive: a worker reporting less than the action asks for is skipped for that action, whatever the admission ledger says. The ledger only subtracts what actions declare; this catches the ones that declared too little. Workers older than v1.7.3 report nothing and are never vetoed."]}]]}]
